1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:05,800
Cheap-Drive: a vehicle-transfer dispatcher tested across 1,165 scored simulator worlds.

2
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:14,800
Every request runs through four rules: screen slack and distance, price by trust, escalate driver pay before warnings, and protect the 90% on-time gate.

3
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:21,800
Every run produces an inspectable offline HTML report reconciling the event stream, financial ledger, and delivery incidents.

4
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:29,800
We kept all 1,155 completed practice runs across six model stages—Baseline, Alpha, Beta Early, Beta Late, Gamma Early, and Gamma Late—including failed experiments.

5
00:00:30,100 --> 00:00:37,800
Tuning is not validation: pushing volume failed gamma-t04 at 89.80%, and Gamma Early's long-route candidate failed its first fresh holdout at 89.956% on time.

6
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:46,800
Revised Gamma—combining notes, repaired pairs, and segment controls—passed all 8 fresh confirmation weeks (v09–v16), adding +€2,031/week (+20.21%) while raising worst on-time to 96.95%.

7
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:53,800
Across two saved five-week official Beta ranking rounds, all 10 weeks qualified: €50,541.26 in Round 5 and €59,528.62 in Round 6.

8
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:59,800
Cheap-Drive: win the right work, deliver it reliably.
